<title>MEXICO: FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 29.11 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 29.11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 141 basis points to 29.11 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     27.70	    29.11		  +141 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     28.79	    29.23		   +44 bps</p>
<p>    181-DAY    28.81	    29.05		   +24 bps</p>
<p>    336-DAY    28.41	    28.71		   +30 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1930 EST.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559</p>
